2026-10-09T02:14:09.1761440Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1771923Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1870546Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1880982Z [0m
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1881510Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1882387Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1883126Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1883661Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1884633Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1885357Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1885808Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1886244Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1886430Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1886906Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1887488Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1887937Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1888291Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1888447Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1888675Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1888932Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1889206Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1889770Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1889900Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1890008Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1890162Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1890517Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1891017Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1893865Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1894031Z I will:
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1894240Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1894639Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1895716Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1896523Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1897216Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1897503Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1897786Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1898542Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1899517Z    /root
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1909935Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1927069Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1928128Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1928983Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1929432Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1929795Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1930426Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1948228Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1949251Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1959281Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1960096Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1960674Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1961027Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1961337Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1961585Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1961879Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1962829Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1963291Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1963476Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1963970Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1964259Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1964548Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T02:14:09.1964893Z   $ sh ./install-nix
